Z||000000||LZeitgeist||03-14-2001||12:51 PM||||Are the skirts on the '84 Indy replicas a bright silver or a darker-than-silver metallic charcoaol/pewter color?<P>'84 Pontiac paint codes list an 84 'Charcoal' and 12,13,16 & 17 'Silver' codes.<P>So are they silver or charcoal?<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 03-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||03-14-2001||09:03 PM||||the code for all the exterior colors should be on driver side fender well inside the front hood-its at the bottom of the label after 'WA'. If your just looking for the color, Id try an auto paint store or a Pontiac dealer to see if they have the code for the indy. If I have the car or access to it, I use a laser color scanner to find a code, most auto paint stores have them. It shoots a laser beam into the paint and reads out matched paint codes from a database.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||03-14-2001||11:27 PM||||Roger - thanks for the suggestions... however, it's a red '88 we're repainting with the '84 color scheme, so the codes listed on the car won't work. We don't have an Indy to look at.<P>The books I've seen at the stores list all the different colors for the 1984 GM or Pontiac colors, but they don't specify what color was used where on what car. They list one charcoal color, but 4 different silver colors for 1984.<P>Were the skirts on the Indys a bright silver color, or more of a darker metallic charcoal or pewter color?||||reg||1
